``` LF-12 | Forwarder Throughput Throttling and Parsing Bottlenecks
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: A forwarder is falling behind on its files with no errors;
    confirm whether it is throttled by maxKBps, and on heavy forwarders, find
    which parsing processor is consuming the most CPU.
    Run on: SH, with the forwarders' _internal forwarded. Replace <heavy_fwd>
    with the forwarder's hostname.
    Query: Main query
    If this returns nothing, run probes/LF-12-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=splunkd earliest=-24h
    (component=ThruputProcessor "maxKBps")
| stats count as throttle_warnings latest(_time) as last_seen by host
| join type=left host
    [search index=_internal source=*metrics.log group=thruput name=thruput
         earliest=-24h
     | stats avg(instantaneous_kbps) as avg_kbps
             max(instantaneous_kbps) as max_kbps by host]
| eval avg_kbps=round(avg_kbps, 0), max_kbps=round(max_kbps, 0)
| convert ctime(last_seen)
| sort - throttle_warnings
| table host throttle_warnings avg_kbps max_kbps last_seen
